  "description": "Do you have to add milk to scrambled eggs? No, but they keep the dish more flavorful and moist. Go on, give it a try.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: 2 tablespoons milk (optional)\n\nOptional substitutions: Freshly ground black pepper → white pepper\n\nNotes: We like to season our eggs with salt at about 1% of their weight, or about 1.5g for 3 large eggs (though we rarely actually measure it out in practice). Just note that not only do different eaters have different salt-level preferences, but the volume of a given weight of salt itself will vary dramatically by brand, so season at your own discretion.",
